column2:
My friend, I have seen a fourth —
10	it goes beyond my three dreams:
11	I caught sight of an Anzû-bird in the sky;
12	it rose and, like a cloud, was gliding over us:
13	[ ... ] its face was warped;
14	its mouth was fire; its breath was deat[h.]
15	A young ma[n too,] strange of fram[e —]
16	[ ... ] he stands there in my night;
17	[ ... ] he seized its wings; he took my arm;
18	[ ... ] he flung it down [bef]ore me;
19	[ ... ] on top of it.

It [rose and, lik]e a cloud, was gl[iding] over us —
a+2	[ ... ] and its face was warped;
a+3	its mouth was fire; its breath was death.
a+4	You — you fear its glowering aura;
a+5	I — I will make you raise(?) your foot upon it(?):
a+6	the young man you saw was mighty Šamaš.
